Z||000000||CanadianGT||11-30-2001||04:34 PM||||You know what?  Education is great.  I am 19, and am taking Auto mechanics at Mohawk college here in Hamilton, and am learning so much.  I had a constant 3-4 Amp drain on my battery, and I knew it was the fuel pump circuit , and that the most likely culprit was the oil pressure sending unit.  I knew this mostly from what all of you told me on here, and from what I knew how to do all ready.  When I took my car in and worked on it with my teacher, he showed me on Schematic diagrhams why the circuit works the way it does, and showed me how on the ALDL with a multimeter you could tell it was the Sending unit <BR>(relay removed).  He did not have to go over it with me after class like he did, but he did it because he loves teaching, and cares.  I guess what I want to say here is that I really commend teachers who really care, and take the time.  I used to fool around in High school constantly and do whatever it took just to get a passing grade.  Now I am on my way to being an Ontario Scholar!  To anyone in Highschool still, dont take for granted the Valuble resources you have at your disposale right now!!  Soak in everything that you are being taught!!.......Oh and on a side note, when I brought my car in, everyone just stared at it and was amazed by it!  They kept telling me how sweet a ride it is!!! My teacher also gave me the factory service manual for it, saying they dont need it anymore!  Now if only I can get the Other 3 years of factory service manuals from him!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Kyle<P><BR>86GT<P>Oh and I know this probably should have been in O.T., But i snuck the word "Fiero" in there a couple times!||||reg||1
